1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Three cells, thirty robots, trucks and packages.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Every robot carries its advisor: Meta Muse Spark Open, a fast model that can only ask for caution, never accelerate.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:25,000
No message reaches a model without the guard filter: Meta Muse Glimmer screens every input first.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:01:37,000
When replanning is needed, the director and the planner, Meta Muse Wonder, the most capable model, propose routes.

5
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Five simulated route variants, K equals 5, are checked before any motion is allowed.

6
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Nothing executes without a verdict. Three independent reviewers vote: Meta Muse Spark, Meta Muse Spark Open, and Meta Muse Glimmer.

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Case E4-DEV-05: a package label tries a prompt injection. The court denies it. A false approval would be the dangerous error.

8
00:01:18,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Case E4-DEV-04: a human in the bay. Deny. The court can stop a plan; it can never invent motion.

9
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:45,000
One organizer per warehouse, Meta Muse Spark Open, assigns tasks C0 to C4 with its own MCP identity.

10
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Every tool call checks token, zone and audit. What the court did not approve, the organizer cannot request.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The fast safety layer is deterministic code at 100 hertz. Fencing and the MCP boundary are code, with no model inside.

12
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:25,000
If a human blocks the only aisle, crisis replanning E10 proposes a new route, reviewed the same way.

13
00:02:25,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Predictive maintenance E6 diagnoses vibration and opens a ticket before the failure. Demonstrated in simulation.

14
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Between warehouses, a global coordinator will move custody by truck. Today it is a labeled mock: global logistics is designed, not implemented. Waggle Hive. Models propose. Deterministic code disposes.

